<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all seven auctions whereby it had sought to drain 6.841 billion pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	400 million  14 days    25.41 pct</p>
<p>	500 million  13 days    25.38 pct</p>
<p>	500 million  12 days    25.28 pct</p>
<p>	1.200 bln   8 days    25.35 pct</p>
<p>	1.300 bln   6 days    25.29 pct</p>
<p>	1.400 bln   5 days    25.40 pct</p>
<p>	1.541 bln   1 day     25.14 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
